[2026/07/18 13:38:37] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_liPxOCCl1MH8f6xA9wI4LzA5', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I will fix the failure by making plotting optional so the LensKit experiment still runs even when matplotlib is unavailable. The script keeps the 80/20 split fixed, varies only the ImplicitMF random seed, computes Recall@20 and NDCG@20 with LensKit, prints a validation-loss proxy each run, and saves all metrics, recommendations, and summary statistics to the working directory as NumPy files. If matplotlib is installed, it will also generate a seed-variation plot; otherwise it will skip plotting gracefully and write a small status file noting that plots were skipped.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport json\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nfrom lenskit import batch\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\\nfrom lenskit.topn import RecListAnalysis\\nfrom lenskit.metrics.topn import recall, ndcg\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'movielens100k\': {\\n        \'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'predictions\': [],\\n        \'ground_truth\': [],\\n        \'seeds\': [],\\n        \'timestamps\': []\\n    }\\n}\\n\\ncols = [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\']\\nratings = pd.read_csv(\'u.data\', sep=\'\\\\t\', names=cols, engine=\'python\')\\nratings = ratings[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\']].copy()\\nratings[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n\\nsplit_seed = 2024\\nrng = np.random.default_rng(split_seed)\\nmask = rng.random(len(ratings)) < 0.8\\ntrain = ratings.loc[mask, [\'user\', \'item\', \'rati